{"id":"effect-9712161d-3b7b-5047-93c3-1d2159feb270","sessionId":"c522c2d8-c314-57f5-3362-1276adb03959","turnId":"turn-92909cbfd49a1589b34ae3f66f7defde","inputEntryId":"user-turn-92909cbfd49a1589b34ae3f66f7defde-1","createdAt":1794285547630,"updatedAt":1794285547637,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.write_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.write_file","display":{"summary":"Writing ANSWER.md","content":"## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function in `src/app.py` returns a Python `float` (via `round(..., 4)`).\nWhen a second story is published, the `related()` function builds a list of similar stories\nwith their `score` values (the float returned by `similarity()`). DynamoDB rejects\nfloat values in items, raising:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\nThe first publish succeeds because the `similar` list is empty (no existing stories to\ncompare against). The second publish fails because `similar` now contains entries with\nfloat `score` values.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `src/app.py`:\n\n1. Added `from decimal import Decimal` at the top of the file.\n2. Modified `similarity()` to return `Decimal(str(round(...)))` instead of a float.\n\nThis ensures the `score` field stored in DynamoDB is a `Decimal` type, which is\nsupported by DynamoDB and will never trigger the float rejection error.\n","suffix":"","verb":"Creating","message":"ANSWER.md","settledVerb":"Created","settledMessage":"ANSWER.md","statusText":"Writing file"},"kind":"file_write","input":{"filePath":"ANSWER.md","content":"## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function in `src/app.py` returns a Python `float` (via `round(..., 4)`).\nWhen a second story is published, the `related()` function builds a list of similar stories\nwith their `score` values (the float returned by `similarity()`). DynamoDB rejects\nfloat values in items, raising:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\nThe first publish succeeds because the `similar` list is empty (no existing stories to\ncompare against). The second publish fails because `similar` now contains entries with\nfloat `score` values.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `src/app.py`:\n\n1. Added `from decimal import Decimal` at the top of the file.\n2. Modified `similarity()` to return `Decimal(str(round(...)))` instead of a float.\n\nThis ensures the `score` field stored in DynamoDB is a `Decimal` type, which is\nsupported by DynamoDB and will never trigger the float rejection error.\n"}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","approvalType":"always","approvalSource":"bypass","durationMs":0.0,"display":{"success":true,"verb":"Created","message":"ANSWER.md","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-Eij7Xi/ANSWER.md","content":"## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function in `src/app.py` returns a Python `float` (via `round(..., 4)`).\nWhen a second story is published, the `related()` function builds a list of similar stories\nwith their `score` values (the float returned by `similarity()`). DynamoDB rejects\nfloat values in items, raising:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\nThe first publish succeeds because the `similar` list is empty (no existing stories to\ncompare against). The second publish fails because `similar` now contains entries with\nfloat `score` values.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `src/app.py`:\n\n1. Added `from decimal import Decimal` at the top of the file.\n2. Modified `similarity()` to return `Decimal(str(round(...)))` instead of a float.\n\nThis ensures the `score` field stored in DynamoDB is a `Decimal` type, which is\nsupported by DynamoDB and will never trigger the float rejection error.\n","fileExisted":false,"previousContent":null},"decision":"execute"}}
